--TEST--
`Core\Response::setHeader` puts no byte in the body, and setting one name twice is admitted rather than refused as a duplicate -- spec § 15
--FILE--
<?nvs
// Like `setStatus` and unlike `rule:security/response-body-is-one-typed-member`'s five body members: this one
// declares and writes nothing. That is why `E0801` does not reach it, and why
// an `echo` beside it is the ordinary spelling rather than two writers
// disagreeing about what the body is.
var $quiet = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    Core\Response::setHeader("X-Request-Id", "9f2");
    Core\Response::setHeader("Cache-Control", "no-store");
});
echo "two calls wrote [", $quiet, "]\n";

// A refused one is quieter still: every check runs before the declaration, so
// a refusal leaves neither a byte nor a header behind. The `catch` inside the
// callable binds its own name -- repeating an enclosing frame's is an ICE in
// the lowerer today, which the playbook owns.
var $onRefusal = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    try {
        Core\Response::setHeader("X Request", "ok");
    } catch (LogicError $unnameable) {
    }
});
echo "a refusal wrote [", $onRefusal, "]\n";

// Set, not add: one name may be written as often as a program likes and the
// last value is the one that answers. Nothing here reads a header back — the
// crossing is asserted in `nvs-server`, where a response exists — so what is
// pinned is that the second and third calls are admitted rather than refused
// as duplicates of the first.
uint $accepted = 0;
uint $i = 0;
while ($i < 3) {
    try {
        Core\Response::setHeader("X-Request-Id", "9f2");
        $accepted = $accepted + 1;
    } catch (LogicError $duplicate) {
    }
    $i = $i + 1;
}
echo "one name set ", $accepted, " times\n";

// And a header beside a body leaves the body alone, byte for byte.
var $withHeader = Core\Out::capture(fn (): void => {
    Core\Response::setHeader("X-Request-Id", "9f2");
    Core\Response::text("created");
});
echo "a body under a header is [", $withHeader, "]\n";
--EXPECT--
two calls wrote []
a refusal wrote []
one name set 3 times
a body under a header is [created]
